{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
\par
{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Creates a custom cursor. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Creates a new custom cursor image that can be set for a window with {\b glfwSetCursor}. The cursor can be destroyed with {\b glfwDestroyCursor}. Any remaining cursors are destroyed by {\b glfwTerminate}.\par
The pixels are 32-bit, little-endian, non-premultiplied RGBA, i.e. eight bits per channel with the red channel first. They are arranged canonically as packed sequential rows, starting from the top-left corner.\par
The cursor hotspot is specified in pixels, relative to the upper-left corner of the cursor image. Like all other coordinate systems in GLFW, the X-axis points to the right and the Y-axis points down.\par
