This function returns the last state reported for the specified key to the specified window. The returned state is one of {\f2 GLFW_PRESS}  or {\f2 GLFW_RELEASE} . The action {\f2 GLFW_REPEAT}  is only reported to the key callback.\par
If the {\b GLFW_STICKY_KEYS} input mode is enabled, this function returns {\f2 GLFW_PRESS}  the first time you call it for a key that was pressed, even if that key has already been released.\par
The key functions deal with physical keys, with {\b key tokens} named after their use on the standard US keyboard layout. If you want to input text, use the Unicode character callback instead.\par
The {\b modifier key bit masks} are not key tokens and cannot be used with this function.\par
{\b Do not use this function}  to implement text input.\par
