{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
\par
{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Sets an input option for the specified window. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This function sets an input mode option for the specified window. The mode must be one of {\b GLFW_CURSOR}, {\b GLFW_STICKY_KEYS}, {\b GLFW_STICKY_MOUSE_BUTTONS}, {\b GLFW_LOCK_KEY_MODS} or {\b GLFW_RAW_MOUSE_MOTION}.\par
If the mode is {\f2 GLFW_CURSOR} , the value must be one of the following cursor modes:{
\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
{\f2 GLFW_CURSOR_NORMAL}  makes the cursor visible and behaving normally.\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
{\f2 GLFW_CURSOR_HIDDEN}  makes the cursor invisible when it is over the content area of the window but does not restrict the cursor from leaving.\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
{\f2 GLFW_CURSOR_DISABLED}  hides and grabs the cursor, providing virtual and unlimited cursor movement. This is useful for implementing for example 3D camera controls.\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
{\f2 GLFW_CURSOR_CAPTURED}  makes the cursor visible and confines it to the content area of the window.\par}
If the mode is {\f2 GLFW_STICKY_KEYS} , the value must be either {\f2 GLFW_TRUE}  to enable sticky keys, or {\f2 GLFW_FALSE}  to disable it. If sticky keys are enabled, a key press will ensure that {\b glfwGetKey} returns {\f2 GLFW_PRESS}  the next time it is called even if the key had been released before the call. This is useful when you are only interested in whether keys have been pressed but not when or in which order.\par
If the mode is {\f2 GLFW_STICKY_MOUSE_BUTTONS} , the value must be either {\f2 GLFW_TRUE}  to enable sticky mouse buttons, or {\f2 GLFW_FALSE}  to disable it. If sticky mouse buttons are enabled, a mouse button press will ensure that {\b glfwGetMouseButton} returns {\f2 GLFW_PRESS}  the next time it is called even if the mouse button had been released before the call. This is useful when you are only interested in whether mouse buttons have been pressed but not when or in which order.\par
If the mode is {\f2 GLFW_LOCK_KEY_MODS} , the value must be either {\f2 GLFW_TRUE}  to enable lock key modifier bits, or {\f2 GLFW_FALSE}  to disable them. If enabled, callbacks that receive modifier bits will also have the {\b GLFW_MOD_CAPS_LOCK} bit set when the event was generated with Caps Lock on, and the {\b GLFW_MOD_NUM_LOCK} bit when Num Lock was on.\par
If the mode is {\f2 GLFW_RAW_MOUSE_MOTION} , the value must be either {\f2 GLFW_TRUE}  to enable raw (unscaled and unaccelerated) mouse motion when the cursor is disabled, or {\f2 GLFW_FALSE}  to disable it. If raw motion is not supported, attempting to set this will emit {\b GLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE}. Call {\b glfwRawMouseMotionSupported} to check for support.\par
